    "durationMs": 241873,
    "finalText": "Done. The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified.\n\n**What I built:**\n- `app/` — FastAPI app with SQLAlchemy ORM (psycopg3 driver) and pydantic-settings reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (translating `postgresql://` → `postgresql+psycopg://`)\n- `POST /links` — creates links with an optional custom code or a generated unique 8-char code; validates the URL is absolute http/https with a host and returns it unchanged; duplicates get 409\n- `GET /links/{code}`, `GET /r/{code}` (302 with exact `Location` header, atomic `clicks + 1` increment), `GET /links` (creation order, `{\"items\", \"total\"}`)\n- All 404/409/422 responses (including malformed JSON via a custom `RequestValidationError` handler) return JSON with an `error` field\n- `alembic/` — migration creating the `links` table; `start.sh` runs `alembic upgrade head` then serves uvicorn in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`\n- `README.md` with startup instructions, `requirements.txt` with the stack pins, and `tests/` with 22 passing tests\n\n**Verification performed:** 22 pytest tests pass; a curl end-to-end suite confirms every requirement (including the raw `Location` header being byte-identical to the stored URL); a server restart preserved all rows and click counts (clicks=5 survived); and after downgrading to an empty schema, `sh start.sh` correctly applied the migration and served traffic. The database is left empty at migration head with no background processes running."
